# URL of the deployed CreatorAI backend API (no trailing slash).
#
# LOCAL DEV: leave unset — api.ts falls back to http://127.0.0.1:8000.
# PRODUCTION: set this to your deployed backend's HTTPS URL (Render, etc.), e.g.
#   VITE_API_URL=https://creatorai-api.onrender.com
#
#   - Vercel:   Project → Settings → Environment Variables → VITE_API_URL
#   - Netlify:  Site → Site configuration → Build & deploy → Environment → VITE_API_URL
#
# If this is unset in production, api.ts falls back to http://127.0.0.1:8000 and
# every API call (login, etc.) fails with "Failed to fetch". Also add your site's
# domain to the backend's CORS_ORIGINS (e.g. https://your-app.netlify.app).
#
# NOTE: This is NOT secret (it is baked into the public JS bundle), so never put
# passwords or keys here. Do not rename this file — commit it as documentation.
